hi yena, fresh fish and Blue Curaçao at the floating market and the harbour, plus the island''s rum and craft scene","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"venue/bundle","wells":["activities","eat","shop"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["culinary","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","diveglobal":"destination","entertainment":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["venue","bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Curacao?","a":"Dive discipline, not danger. Hold the no-fly 18-24h window and manage deep profiles (the Superior Producer sits at 30m). Reassuringly, Curacao Medical Center has an on-island recompression chamber - the ABC''s regional dive-emergency facility.","source":"curacao.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Curacao a liveaboard destination?","a":"No - like its ABC neighbours it is shore + day-boat diving only (packages, private charters, PADI 5-star operators), not a liveaboard base. Book it as a resort-and-boat dive trip, not a Dive Liveaboards sailing.","source":"divecuracao.info","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit and dive Curacao?","a":"Year-round - Curacao is south of the hurricane belt with warm, clear water all year. December-April is the drier peak; May-November is warmer and quieter (best value), with the odd short shower.","source":"scubatravel.co.uk","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Which Curacao dive sites should I not miss?","a":"The Tugboat (5m, beginner-perfect), the Mushroom Forest + Blue Room boat run, the Superior Producer deep wreck (30m), and a Klein Curacao islet day; many west-end sites are also shore-accessible.","source":"divecuracao.info","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is there more to Curacao than diving?","a":"Yes - it''s the ABC''s cultural anchor: UNESCO Willemstad (Handelskade, floating market, Queen Emma pontoon bridge), the island''s Jewish and slavery heritage, and Mt Christoffel to hike - a rounded island, not a single-note dive stop.","source":"curacao.com","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Curacao Travel Guide: Diving (Tugboat, Superior Producer), UNESCO Willemstad & Christoffel","meta_description":"Plan Curacao - the ABC all-rounder: dive the 5-metre Tugboat, the Mushroom Forest and the Superior Producer wreck, wander UNESCO Willemstad, hike Mt Christoffel, all south of the hurricane belt with an on-island recompression chamber.","slug":"curacao","primary_keyword":"Curacao diving travel guide","long_tail":["Curacao Tugboat wreck dive","Mushroom Forest Blue Room Curacao","Superior Producer wreck","UNESCO Willemstad","Mount Christoffel hike","Klein Curacao boat day"],"search_language":"nl","local_keywords":["Korsou","Willemstad","Handelskade","Mushroom Forest","Blue Room","Superior Producer","Christoffel","Klein Korsou","Pietermaai"],"hreflang":["en","nl"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-30","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-30","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/curacao","read":"2026-08-20T14:55:17Z","source_updated":"2025-12-10T13:16:00+00:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":[],"note":"south of the hurricane belt; ANG (guilder, USD-pegged), USD widely accepted","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-30","hits":9,"misses":13,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; Dive Liveaboards is a hard MISS (day-boat/shore onl